thub.com/users/jlink/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlink/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlink/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlink/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlink/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2016-03-16T21:20:01Z","updated_at":"2016-03-16T21:20:01Z","body":"@sbrannen It's definitely a bug that should be fixed.\n\nBut it also makes me think that if we have to rely on the order of registration something in our extension mechanism could be improved to make order of registration less relevant. The order should only matter if two extensions compete about the order of an extension point being applied.\n\nIn the example from SpringExtension that triggered the issue: Could the problem be circumvented by choosing an appropriate `Position` value when registering the conflicting extension points in the extensions?\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/junit-team/junit-framework/issues/comments/197553838/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"jlink","id":103937,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwMzkzNw==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/103937?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlink","html_url":"https://github.com/jlink","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlink/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlink/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlink/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlink/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlink/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlink/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlink/repos","events_ur