om/jlink","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlink/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlink/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlink/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlink/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlink/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlink/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlink/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlink/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlink/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"performed_via_github_app":null},{"id":593034922,"node_id":"MDEyOkxhYmVsZWRFdmVudDU5MzAzNDkyMg==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/junit-team/junit-framework/issues/events/593034922","actor":{"login":"jlink","id":103937,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwMzkzNw==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/103937?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlink","html_url":"https://github.com/jlink","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlink/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlink/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlink/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlink/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlink/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlink/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlink/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlink/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlink/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"event":"labeled","commit_id":null,"commit_url":null,"created_at":"2016-03-17T08:04:27Z","label":{"name":"in progress","color":"eb6420"},"performed_via_github_app":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/junit-team/junit-framework/issues/comments/197768241","html_url":"https://github.com/junit-team/junit-framework/issues/208#issuecomment-197768241","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/junit-team/junit-framework/issues/208","id":197768241,"node_id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDE5Nzc2ODI0MQ==","user":{"login":"jlink","id":103937,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwMzkzNw==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/103937?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlink","html_url":"https://github.com/jlink","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlink/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlink/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlink/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlink/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlink/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlink/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlink/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlink/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlink/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2016-03-17T08:48:29Z","updated_at":"2016-03-17T08:50:41Z","body":"After revisiting the current implementation (https://github.com/junit-team/junit5/blob/master/junit-commons/src/main/java/org/junit/gen5/commons/util/AnnotationUtils.java#L144-L229) I'm not so sure anymore, we should fix it. The algorithm is already complicated enough. Adding the behaviour suggested in the description would add even more complexity and just open the can of other corner cases, for example:\n\n``` java\n    @ExtendWith(A.class)\n    class BaseTests {\n    }\n\n    @ExtendWith(B.class)\n    @ExtendWith(A.class)\n    class ExtendedTests extends BaseTests {\n    }\n```\n\nWhat's more intuitive: `A.class` being registered before `B.class` or after `B.class`? Consider that the author of `ExtendedTests` might not be aware of `BaseTests` already having `A.class` as extension - or it is added after the fact. Even worse, what's intuitive for `@ExtendWith` might not be intuitive for `@Tag` and we'll have to make the order configurable. \n\nIn order to fix the underlying issue, extensions shouldn't rely on the order of registration. My hope is that with the approach in #135 most of these problems could be solved by adding approriate values for `Position`. Maybe we will need a different kind of position constraints between extensions, like `Position.before(A.class, B.class)`. And now we're back in the discussion about #112.\n\nSo my vote is for not fixing this and instead concentrate on eventually come to grips with #135 and #112.\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/junit-team/junit-framework/issues/comments/197768241/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"jlink","id":103937,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwMzkzNw==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/103937?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlink","html_url":"https://github.com/jlink","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlink/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlink/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlink/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlink/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlink/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlink/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlink/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlink/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlink/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false}},{"id":593276135,"node_id":"MDE1OlJlZmVyZW5jZWRFdmVudDU5MzI3NjEzNQ==","url":"https://api.github.